course: dictionary
lesson: 709
title: Many meanings, one clue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Bare is a good example. Read the words around it to choose the right meaning. «Ice on bare skin can burn» tells you bare means not covered, because the skin has no clothes or covering over it.
explain: «Broken glass ... is never picked up with bare hands.» Bare hands means hands with no gloves or tools. Check by swapping in your meaning: "never picked up with uncovered hands" still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: «Pushed back, it leaves the forehead bare.» Here bare means uncovered, with nothing on top. Bare can also be a verb, as in an animal baring its teeth, which means showing them by uncovering them. The clues in the sentence always tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Bare can be an adjective (bare, barer, barest) or a verb (bare, bares, bared, baring).
fact: «Bare» means not covered by clothes, as in «bare feet» or «bare arms».
fact: «Bare» can mean empty or with nothing on it, as in «bare trees» in winter when the leaves have fallen.
fact: «Bare» can mean just the smallest amount, as in «the bare minimum», which is the least you can do.
fact: «To bare» something means to show it by uncovering it, like an animal «baring its teeth» as a warning.
exercise: «Ice or frozen peas should be wrapped in a cloth, because ice on bare skin can burn.» What does bare mean here? | *Not covered by clothes | Only just enough | Shown by uncovering | Empty, with nothing on it
exercise: «A helmet ... pushed back, it leaves the forehead bare.» What does bare mean here? | Very fast | Loud and noisy | *Uncovered, with nothing over it | Cold and wet
exercise: «Broken glass ... never picked up with bare hands.» What does bare hands mean? | With both hands at once | Quickly, in a hurry | With very dirty hands | *Without gloves or tools
test: «The Great Wall of China ... is practically impossible to see with bare eyes from orbit.» What does bare eyes mean? | Eyes that are closed | Eyes shut tight | *Eyes without any tools or help | Eyes that are red
test: «The dog bared its teeth at the stranger.» What does bared mean? | Licked clean | *Showed by uncovering | Hid behind a tree | Barked loudly
exam: Which meaning of bare fits «bare winter trees» best? | *Empty, with no leaves on them | Covered in snow | Very tall | Painted bright green
